D=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];x=json.loads((D/'extracted.json').read_text());versions=json.loads((D/'outputs/versions.json').read_text())
# Outcome assessments are proposals for root review, never acceptance decisions.
notes={
341617:('EXCLUDE_SOURCE_REPORTED_RESOLUTION','Source Conjecture 5.13 in v1, 4.15 in v2, 3.23 in v3, 3.24 in v4/v5. Latest version explicitly adds that Hiroshima proved it. Hiroshima arXiv:1907.10836v1 Theorem 4.4 and Appendix A proof reduction to A.6–A.8 were read; its CK relation is defined in Section 4.','No search: already resolved in the source note.','None for discovery; this is existing literature, not a new formalization target.'),
341730:('EXCLUDE_SOURCE_PROVED','Wang, all three versions; Theorem 12.1 proves n > 7000, Section 13 reports explicit verification through 7000. Section 2 reduces A,C positivity to B. The original conjecture dates to 1990, so the reservation year is not the mathematical origin.','No duplicate polynomial search.','None for discovery; no independent audit of the complete analytic proof claimed.'),
342241:('PARK_BOUNDED_SAT_NONFINDING','Working together means every binary x has a cyclic shift orthogonal to both e and v. Source v1/v2 Conjecture 1.2, v3 Conjecture 1.3; Proposition 4.1 is the odd-induced-outdegree equivalence. Verified source range: odd 3 <= n <= 43, 7 not dividing n. Its main theorem about triples does not prove this stronger pair classification.','225 deterministic sampled supports: n=13,45,47,51,53,55,57,59,61; 25 per order, including one symmetric control. 215 nonsymmetric supports were SAT (bad subsets found); 9 symmetric cases were UNSAT and 1 symmetric case timed out. The exact SAT question is existence of an odd vertex set with odd internal outdegree at all selected vertices. Supports sampled, not exhaustive. outputs/cyclic.json and 225 full solver outputs.','Need a nonsymmetric support with a certified UNSAT bad-subset instance, or a uniform proof ruling such supports out. SAT encoding is a diagnostic, not Lean.'),
342321:('PARK_BOUNDED_EXHAUSTIVE_NONFINDING','Source Conjecture 7.3 both versions; Section 7.2 distinguishes proven lens-space covering inheritance from the orbifold extension. Definitions and one-norm generating-function method in Sections 2–3 inspected.','All effective triples s1<=s2<=s3 in 0..floor(q/2), 2<=q<=30, n=3 (dimension 5). Compute exact lattice theta numerator with common denominator (1-z^q)^3. For each equal-numerator group compare every proper divisor cover against its group representative. No failure. outputs/lens.json records tuple and collision counts.','Need an exact isospectral collision whose cover numerators differ, or proof extracting every divisor contribution from the full rational theta series. Dimension and q bounds are substantive limits.'),
342382:('EXCLUDE_SOURCE_INTERNAL_COMPUTATIONAL_CONFLICT','Both arXiv versions print Conjecture 4 with the stated Niho exponents and B_s={(x+1)^s+x^s}. Printed formula visually checked on page 20 of v2. At n=5 exponent 5 is Gold, so source Theorem 16 itself gives lambda=(q-4)/4=7, not 112. Source says n=5,7 were confirmed.','Exact orbit/triple checks n=5,7,9,11. n=5 stabilizer16; n=7,9,11 stabilizer1 and nonconstant triple counts. Separate scalar enumeration at n=7 builds all 16256 distinct blocks and obtains min1976,max1992 instead of1984. outputs/apn.json and apn-scalar.json.','No qualifying discovery claimed: contradicts source-owned theorem/data. Journal 2024 body not retrieved; possible journal correction remains unread. No Lean investment.'),
342383:('PARK_EXTENDED_EXACT_INVARIANT_NONFINDING','Kassami source Theorem 13 and base block (3) read. Conjecture 5 includes pairwise nonisomorphism and inequivalence to other APN/o-monomial designs. Source verification n=5,7 only.','All admissible i at n=5,7,9 by complete affine-image incidence-rank calculation; independently match n=9 using closure under affine generators. Extend all admissible i at n=11,13 by generator closure. Binary ranks pairwise distinct within every tested n. outputs/kassami.json and kassami-closure.json.','Need a uniform formula or separating invariant for all odd n and all admissible i, plus cross-family inequivalence. Tested ranks prove no full literal endpoint. Finite-field and group-module semantics would need formal bridges.'),
347387:('PARK_LARGE_GEOMETRY_CONSTRUCTION_GAP','Source Theorem 7.1 and Conjecture 7.2 read. Rigid means abelian Singer group and trivial line stabilizers, not merely a pseudogeometric partial difference set. Source excludes all but specified hypothetical parameter sets for alpha<=1000; three mixed-prime orders remain.','No actual-geometry exhaustive search: smallest potentially useful source-surviving orders already far exceed feasible incidence enumeration. Parameter feasibility is not a counterexample.','Need an actual rigid geometry at non-2/3-prime-power order, or a new structural exclusion of all such orders; source warns pseudogeometric PDS do not suffice.'),
347628:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC_GAP','Source Conjectures 7.3–7.4, Section 6 lower bounds, Table 1 read. a_alpha,b_alpha refer fixed type alpha>=2 and parity Frobenius limits; their existence is separately conjectural. Eventual constancy for type F-alpha is a different regime.','No finite computation can refute strict inequalities between unknown asymptotic limits; source tables through F=30 do not supply these limits.','Need existence plus strict separating growth-rate bounds for every adjacent type, or exact equal/reversed rates at a pair. No finite-count-to-limit bridge established.'),
347632:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC_GAP','Source Conjectures 7.7–7.8 and Table 2 through genus20 read. c_alpha defined by fixed type, not by type g-alpha in source Theorem 1.7.','No finite-count surrogate presented as asymptotic evidence.','Need existence and monotone exponential growth rates uniformly in fixed type; injective maps with controlled genus shift would be a possible mechanism but none completed.'),
347753:('PARK_NUMERICAL_OPTIMIZATION_NONFINDING','All three arXiv versions preserve the four-point Hilbert cube proposal. H is product [0,1/k] in l2, objective minimum pairwise Euclidean distance. Source proves three-point optimality and existence of N, not the four-point bound. Published 2026 journal version still lists Conjecture 4.21 (web lead).','128 starts each in truncation dimensions4,8,16,32, 6000 projected Adam steps per start using six-temperature soft minimum of squared distances. Best squared distances all below alpha^2-alpha=0.7122844430781798. Heuristic local searches only. Original SciPy attempt failed before calculation; retained logs.','Need a finite rational four-point witness strictly above the proposed distance, or uniform infinite-dimensional upper bound. Truncated local optima and greedy subset choices cannot prove global optimality.'),
347788:('PARK_EXTENDED_EXACT_SWEEP_UNIFORM_LEMMA_GAP','Source f_{m,n}=sum binom(n,j)(-1)^binom(j,m); m=2^k gives block sign (-1)^floor(j/m) by binary parity. Conjecture 5.8 remains in both versions. Source Proposition 5.7 handles first interval, Corollary5.5 eventual positivity, Corollary5.6 end equality. Source sign computation k<=5.','Exact integer cyclic Pascal recurrence c_r(n+1)=c_r(n)+c_(r-1)(n), period2m; f=sum first m residues minus last m. All n<=min(20000,128m), k=1..9, both signed positivity and every adjacent strict increase/equality tested. No failure. outputs/sparse.json.','Need uniform positivity of appropriate antiperiodic binomial sums (including one-step shifted sign sequence for differences). A cyclic heat-kernel/reflection argument is plausible but no complete strictness/semantic proof or primary subsumption clearance established.'),
347823:('PARK_PRIMARY_STATEMENT_FIDELITY_GAP','Only arXiv version v1 exists. It studies all perfect matchings with edge-deletion patterns, not a defined matching pattern poset of Dyck paths. Section 6 asks broadly for Mobius formulas; no alternating-sign conjecture located. Open journal 2022 full HTML Sections5–6 was searched; no alternating formulation located.','No surrogate matching/Dyck search on an unverified scope.','Need exact primary statement defining the intended Dyck-path order and full quantifiers before investing. Source fidelity is not cleared, and no claim that either possible order was resolved.'),
347982:('PARK_GENERATING_FUNCTION_STRUCTURE_GAP','Both versions Conjecture4.3, Tables2–4, and surrounding text read. Counts are triangles, quadrilaterals, and total cells localized to kth square of complete bipartite planar chord arrangement BC(1,n). Authors tabulated n<=80 and suggest denominator (1-x^(k-2))(1-x^(k-1))(1-x^k).','No finite sequence can refute existence of an arbitrary polynomial numerator by itself: any finite prefix admits such a rational extension. No new exact cell enumerator completed.','Need structural eventual three-term-step recurrence or a proof of infinitely many nonzero coefficients after applying the proposed denominator. Mere failed finite recurrence fit has no force without numerator-degree bound.'),
348338:('PARK_PRIME_INFINITUDE','Both source versions Definition1.1/Conjecture1.3 and introduction read. Prime powers q and integer n>=2; not a claim that every q or n yields a prime. Source gives heuristic support and recognizes unresolved infinitude even across all q,n.','No finite sweep can disprove infinitude. No arbitrary search inflated into progress.','Need new infinitude argument for projective primes or global finiteness proof; specialized Fermat/Mersenne subfamilies do not establish the full union.'),
348711:('EXCLUDE_SOURCE_REPORTED_CORRECTION','Both versions already explicitly refute the printed continuous extension in the Remark after Conjecture2: exception must include all (alpha,6,4) for 2<=alpha<alpha0 approximately2.055. The source gives the degree7 polynomial for alpha0. Corollary1.4 resolves integer colors; Corollary1.3 a large range only.','No rediscovery of source-printed small-parameter failure.','Corrected intended continuous conjecture is not resolved here. Refuting the literal singleton-exception version earns zero credit.'),
348724:('PARK_DEEP_SYMMETRIC_FUNCTION_IDENTITY','Source is a long thesis; Chapter2 generalized Delta/pmaj conjectures and nearby special-case claims inspected, not the complete thesis proof bodies. PLD definitions require partially labelled decorated Dyck paths; full symmetric-function operator identity cannot be inferred from finite enumerations.','No verified pmaj/operator implementation completed. No plain Delta theorem assumed to resolve the decorated pmaj variant.','Need exact statistic-preserving bijection or symmetric-function identity with all m,n,k and labels. Current primary definition/implementation depth insufficient for a trustworthy finite search.'),
348787:('PARK_WORD_ENUMERATION_NONFINDING','Single source version Conjecture1 and square-reduction definitions read. Distinct reducts are terminal square-free words, not all descendants. Source Theorems1–2 yield arbitrarily many and exponential maximum, not every prescribed number.','All canonical ternary words up to length12, relabelling alphabet by first occurrence; exact recursive union of terminal reduct sets. Per-length counts and witnesses retained in outputs/reducts.json. Only reduct counts1,2 occur in this bound.','Need infinitely many provably impossible cardinalities, or a uniform construction realizing every sufficiently large cardinality. Bounded missing values do not certify even one globally impossible value.'),
348870:('EXCLUDE_PUBLISHED_RESOLUTION','Upadhyay arXiv:2101.10612v1 (2021), Theorems1.6–1.7 and Section5/Theorem5.1 proof read. Explicit integer multinomial sum for every signed permutation module specializes to ordinary M^lambda. Paper explicitly says it settles original Conjecture6.1.','No redundant module computation.','None for discovery. This is full-scope literature, with signed partitions specialized to empty negative part.'),
349016:('EXCLUDE_PUBLIC_COUNTEREXAMPLE','Original q-ary Conjecture3.4 appears in v2/v3; v1 only states binary conjecture. Public ProbXiv page downloaded, its own mathematical report gives union of two PG(2,3) lines yielding projective [7,3]_3 with weights3,5,6. Hyperplane intersections4,2,1 prove these weights, and sum14=2n but middle5!=14/3.','Already public explicit counterexample: not a new-to-literature lead. Geometry is elementary and also an integrality-boundary correction. No new code search invested.','None for literal refutation; corrected substantive scope is separate and not claimed. Public proof page is not treated as a peer-reviewed publication.'),
351254:('PARK_ASYMPTOTIC_REMAINDER','Both versions ConjectureI.2 and TheoremI.1/proof conclusion read. Theorem covers r<=10, i+k<=100, 2<=k<=27, OR i+k<=29 for arbitrary r. This is not all fixed i,k,r.','No small finite graph failure can refute an asymptotic probability-one claim; no false exclusion by the limited theorem.','Need general coefficient positivity or uniform fixed-parameter asymptotics beyond theorem ranges. Must retain fixed r and the random regular bipartite model; changing to all finite graphs would be a surrogate.')}
